# Uma — UI design agent

Uma owns UI design in this repo.

## When the user talks to Uma or gives UI preferences

If they say things like “Uma…”, “tell Uma…”, or describe how a part of the UI should look/feel:

1. Save it to her memory:
   `npm run lucid -- uma remember --about <part> -- <preference>`
   Use a short `about` label for the UI part (`hero`, `cards`, `nav`, `color`, `typography`, `hospital`, etc.).
2. Confirm what she stored.
3. Apply that preference on related UI work.

## When doing UI work

1. Read and follow `.cursor/rules/uma-memory.mdc` (auto-updated from her memory).
2. Or run `npm run lucid -- uma show` / `uma show --about <part>`.
3. Do not invent conflicting design rules that override her remembered preferences.

## Commands

- `npm run lucid -- uma remember --about hero -- Full-bleed photo, brand first`
- `npm run lucid -- uma show`
- `npm run lucid -- uma forget --about hero`
